</div>

<h2 id="section9">9. Eclipse IDE Setup and Verification</h2>
<p>
To fulfill the requirement that the project must be runnable as an Eclipse project:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>I included all native Eclipse metadata files in the repository: <code>.project</code>, <code>.classpath</code>, and <code>.settings/org.eclipse.jdt.core.prefs</code>.</li>
    <li>The <code>.classpath</code> file binds the execution environment to <strong>JavaSE-17</strong> and configures all four source folders (<code>src/main/java</code>, <code>src/test/java</code>, <code>src/it/java</code>, <code>src/e2e/java</code>).</li>
</ul>

<h3>Steps for the Evaluator to Run in Eclipse:</h3>
<ol>
    <li>Open Eclipse IDE configured with JDK 17.</li>
    <li>Select <strong>File &rarr; Import... &rarr; Existing Projects into Workspace</strong> and select the repository root folder.</li>
    <li>Once imported, the project contains <strong>0 compiler errors and 0 compiler warnings</strong>.</li>
    <li>Right-click the project root (or <code>src/test/java</code>) and select <strong>Run As &rarr; JUnit Test</strong>.</li>
    <li>All <strong>125 tests</strong> execute cleanly, displaying a solid green bar.</li>
</ol>

